---
title: 'Annotations'
enterprise: true
---

To improve data analysis, a range of annotations can be applied to Cartesian charts. TThese annotations are especially useful for highlighting trends and key data points.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Annotations" name="simple-annotations" type="generated" /%}

In the example above:

-   Select annotations from the toolbar and click on the series area to add them.
-   Use the floating options toolbar to adjust their position, color, or style.
-   Remove annotations either via the main toolbar (to delete all) or the floating toolbar (to delete individually).

## Annotation Types

A subset of annotation types is available across all Cartesian charts, including:

-   **[Text Annotations](./financial-charts-toolbar/#annotations)**: `text`, `comment`, `callout` and `note`.
-   **[Lines](./financial-charts-toolbar/#lines)**: `line`, `horizontal-line` and `vertical-line`. For charts with vertical [Number Axes](./axes-types/#number), the `parallel-channel` and `disjoint-channel` are also available.
-   **[Arrows](./financial-charts-toolbar/#arrows)**: `arrow`, `arrow-up` and `arrow-down`

## Toolbar

The Annotations Toolbar offers menu options for annotating charts. By default, the toolbar is enabled, but it can be disabled by setting `toolbar.enabled` to `false`.

The menu items in the toolbar can be cutomised by configuring the `toolbar.buttons` options array.

```js
annotations: {
    toolbar: {
        buttons: [
            {
                icon: 'delete',
                value: 'clear',
            },
            {
                icon: 'text-annotation',
                value: 'text-menu',
            },
        ],
    },
},
```

{% chartExampleRunner title="Annotations Toolbar" name="annotations-toolbar" type="generated" /%}

## Keyboard Shortcuts

The following keyboard shortcuts can be used.

-   {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%}+{% kbd "Z"/%} / {% kbd "⌘"/%}+{% kbd "Z"/%} will undo any drawing and annotation actions.
-   {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%}+{% kbd "Y"/%} / {% kbd "⌘"/%}+{% kbd "Y"/%} will redo any undo actions.
-   {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%}+{% kbd "C"/%} / {% kbd "⌘"/%}+{% kbd "C"/%} will copy the selected drawing or annotation.
-   {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%}+{% kbd "V"/%} / {% kbd "⌘"/%}+{% kbd "V"/%} will paste the copied drawing or annotation.
-   {% kbd "Delete"/%} or {% kbd "⌫ Backspace" /%} will delete the selected item.
-   Arrow keys ({% kbd "←"/%} {% kbd "↑"/%} {% kbd "→"/%} {% kbd "↓"/%}) will move the selected drawing or annotation by 1 pixel.  
    Use in combination with {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%} or {% kbd "⇧ Shift"/%} to move by 10 pixels.
-   Holding down {% kbd "⇧ Shift"/%} whilst creating a drawing or dragging a handle will snap it to the nearest 45° angle.

## Save & Restore

Drawings and Annotations can be saved, restored and programmatically initialised and modified, using the [Chart State API](./api-state/).

## Customisation

{% chartExampleRunner title="Annotation Customisation" name="annotations-customisation" type="generated" /%}

To customise the look of Drawings and Annotations, use [Theme Override Options](/themes-api/#reference-AgChartTheme-overrides-common-annotations).

```ts
theme: {
    overrides: {
        common: {
            annotations: {
                line: {
                    stroke: 'lime',
                    strokeWidth: 1,
                    lineDash: [3, 1],
                },
                arrow: {
                    stroke: 'red',
                    strokeWidth: 1,
                    text: {
                        fontSize: 12,
                    },
                },
                text: {
                    color: 'blue',
                    fontSize: 12,
                },
            },
        },
    },
},
```

